('cup-and-handle', 'Cup and Handle', 'A longer recovery and a smaller pause precede an attempted breakout.

Interpretation
continuation · conditional

Context
Usually a rounded consolidation in an uptrend; inverse version is bearish.

Recognition
• Rounded cup instead of one sharp V.
• smaller handle near the rim.
• inverse mirrors shape and direction.

Confirmation to study
Regular: close above handle and rim. Inverse: close below corresponding support.

What weakens the scenario
Regular: loss of handle low. Inverse: break above handle high.

Target framework
Cup depth can be projected from the rim breakout. Consider handle failure and nearer price obstacles before the projection.

Common mistakes and limitations
• A deep or prolonged handle can indicate a different structure.

Also called
• Cup with Handle
• Inverted Cup and Handle

Timeframe
Use completed candles from one consistent timeframe. Session boundaries, liquidity, costs and noise affect interpretation.

Not backtested; no success-rate claim.', 'chart', '[{"label":"Cup with handle","kind":"line","values":[112,104,98,95,96,100,106,112,107,109,116],"guides":[[0,112,10,112]],"note":"Synthetic swing schematic. Final segment shows one possible breakout, not a forecast. Time spacing is simplified."},{"label":"Inverted cup with handle","kind":"line","values":[88,96,102,105,104,100,94,88,93,91,84],"guides":[[0,88,10,88]],"note":"Synthetic swing schematic. Final segment shows one possible breakout, not a forecast. Time spacing is simplified."}]', 112),
