Interpretation
reversal-or-continuation · conditional

Context
Within a trend or near a turning area.

Recognition
• Both boundaries slope in the same direction and converge.
• rising version has higher highs and lows.
• falling version has lower highs and lows.

Confirmation to study
Rising wedge: close below lower boundary. Falling wedge: close above upper boundary.

What weakens the scenario
Failed break back inside; opposite-boundary break further contradicts scenario.

Target framework
The shape supplies no reliable fixed target. In a hypothetical study, compare nearby opposing support or resistance with the planned risk distance.

Common mistakes and limitations
• Wedges may reverse or continue trends. Parallel channels are a different structure.

